From: Balázs Gyimesi <gyimesi.balazs@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nss_rmnet_rx: let paged frags through, leave GRO segments to the stack

The bind handler linearized every non-linear packet before framing it. A
frag list has to be flattened, since the firmware cannot hand it back, but
paged frags are what a zero-copy rmnet deaggregation produces and what
nss_core_send_buffer() already sends as a scatter-gather chain; linearize
only the former.

A device that delivers through GRO (rmnet) also hands the handler merged
segments. The firmware returns one it does not accelerate as a single
packet whose checksum state is gone, and TCP then verifies a checksum over
the merged payload and drops it: TcpInCsumErrors on every host-bound flow
through a QMAP link. Leave merged segments to the stack; a flow that is
accelerated never comes back this way.
---
--- a/nss_rmnet_rx.c
+++ b/nss_rmnet_rx.c
@@ -972,7 +972,22 @@
 	 * zero: the source interface comes from the node pair and any
 	 * forwarding decision from the rule.
 	 */
-	if (skb_is_nonlinear(skb) && skb_linearize(skb)) {
+	/*
+	 * A segment GRO merged: the firmware would return it as one packet
+	 * without its checksum state, and TCP would verify the checksum over
+	 * the merged payload. The stack handles it; an accelerated flow never
+	 * comes back this way.
+	 */
+	if (skb_is_gso(skb)) {
+		return RX_HANDLER_PASS;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * A frag list the firmware could not hand back, so it is flattened;
+	 * paged frags go down as a scatter-gather chain when the device
+	 * advertises SG, and nss_core linearizes them otherwise.
+	 */
+	if (skb_has_frag_list(skb) && skb_linearize(skb)) {
 		return RX_HANDLER_PASS;
 	}
 
